---
title: Web
description: How the Next.js client is laid out, its layers, and its conventions
---

# Web

The client is a Next.js App Router app with one page and one API route. The page holds the chat panel, the map canvas, and the detail drawer. The route runs the agent.

## Stack

- Next.js 15 with the App Router
- The Vercel AI SDK for the chat stream and the tool loop
- Tailwind with the tokens from `canon/DESIGN.md`
- shadcn/ui for the drawer, inputs, and menus
- MapLibre GL for the canvas, reading tiles from a PMTiles file
- zod for every tool input and every service response
- Vitest and Testing Library, with Playwright kept for a release check

## Layout

```plaintext
web/
├── app/
│   ├── page.tsx                # the one page, laying out the three surfaces
│   ├── layout.tsx              # fonts, theme, and providers
│   └── api/chat/route.ts       # the agent route
├── components/
│   ├── chat/
│   │   ├── ChatPanel.tsx       # message list and input
│   │   ├── ToolCall.tsx        # one folded tool call with input and result
│   │   └── QuestionInput.tsx   # the research question paste box
│   ├── canvas/
│   │   ├── MapCanvas.tsx       # map, pins, edges, drag
│   │   ├── Pin.tsx             # one visit pin
│   │   └── LayoutMenu.tsx      # the reader's layout switch
│   └── drawer/
│       ├── VisitDrawer.tsx     # the detail drawer
│       └── CountTable.tsx      # species counts for one visit
├── lib/
│   ├── agent/                  # tools, prompt, models, mode
│   ├── canvas/                 # reducer, layouts, bridge, storage
│   ├── service/                # typed client for the FastAPI service
│   └── visits/                 # the client cache for visit records
├── evals/
├── scripts/
└── test/
    ├── snapshots/              # mock service responses, generated
    └── route/                  # chat route tests against the snapshots
```

## Conventions

- Components read state through hooks in `lib/`, never by importing the reducer or the cache directly
- Every service call goes through `lib/service/`, which parses the response with zod before returning it
- Server-only code sits under `app/api/` or in files marked with `import 'server-only'`
- Tool files export the tool and its zod schema, so tests can build inputs from the schema
- One component per file, named as the file

## Anti-patterns

- Fetching the service from a component. Use the hooks in `lib/visits/`.
- Storing a visit record in canvas state. Store the id and read the record from the cache.
- Adding a tool without adding its name to the canvas bridge, when it is a canvas tool.
- Reading `process.env` in a client component. Pass the value from the server or use a `NEXT_PUBLIC_` variable.

## Scripts

| Script           | What it does                                              |
| ---------------- | --------------------------------------------------------- |
| `lint`           | ESLint                                                    |
| `typecheck`      | `tsc --noEmit`                                            |
| `test`           | Vitest, unit and component                                |
| `test:route`     | The chat route against the mock snapshots                 |
| `snapshots`      | Regenerates the mock snapshots from a local service       |
| `e2e`            | Playwright against a built client and a running service   |
| `build`          | `next build`                                              |
| `start`          | `next start`, used by the root `serve:web` script         |
| `dev`            | Prints a pointer to `serve:web` and exits                 |

## Provider switching

The reader picks a provider in the chat panel's menu. The choice travels as the `X-Model-Provider` header and is kept in `localStorage`, so it survives a reload. `agent.md` covers how the route maps it to a model.

## Deploy

The client deploys through the Vercel integration on every push to `main`. `deploy.md` covers the rewrites and the domain.
